chronymon (1.0.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Kiosk: each axis fits the bulk of what it draws; outliers are
    pinned to the edge, marked and counted.
  * An asinh axis never prints one tick label over another.
  * Temperature gives r squared beside r.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:04:23 -0700

chronymon (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Kiosk: the host's time; room for eight sources and long names.
  * A refclock reference is named, not shown as "-".
  * Status follows chronyd's latest tracking report: no false
    "synchronized" after sync is lost.
  * Unsynchronized, or on the local reference, shaded as a gap.
  * A refclock a PPS is locked to (NMEA) is kept out of the way;
    Sources lines can be hidden by name.
  * "large offset" where makestep would not step.
  * Log ingest survives unreadable, truncated and rewritten files.
  * /api refuses requests that would cost too much.
  * Schemas 4 to 6, migrated on start; logs are reread once.
  * Starts without /run/chrony.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:23:53 -0700

chronymon (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A kiosk page, /kiosk, for an unattended display.
  * chronyd's log fills the charts only where the daemon was not
    recording; the reported line no longer breaks between updates.
  * Sources as chronyd last reported them (schema 3, migrated on start);
    placeholder sources hidden, removed ones listed last, dimmed.
  * /api/sources: `sample` is now `report`, and `removed` is added.

